WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Cylinder geometry. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Calculate swept volume from bore and stroke

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Swept displacement is cylinder area times stroke, multiplied by cylinder count. It describes geometry, not power.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: Illustrative: 86 mm bore × 86 mm stroke × 4 cylinders gives about 1,998 cm³.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Guided unit conversion

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Ideal mechanism only; friction, heat and part-specific behavior need measurements.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Calculate swept volume from bore and stroke
